WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Aisha contacts the insurer after her husband's death.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.160
The producer helps her locate the policy, identify the beneficiary

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.620
designation and obtain the required claim instructions.

4
00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:18.960
The insurer evaluates the claim under the contract and applicable law.

5
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:25.360
Maryland's form-review process generally requires covered life policy forms

6
00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.280
to be filed and approved, subject to stated exceptions.

7
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.160
That oversight does not allow a producer to rewrite a benefit

8
00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:39.260
at claim time. Explain the actual provisions, help the

9
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:44.320
family provide the needed information and avoid promising an outcome before

10
00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:45.620
the facts are reviewed.

11
00:00:46.328 --> 00:00:52.128
An insurer cannot refuse a claim for an arbitrary reason, misrepresent

12
00:00:52.128 --> 00:00:57.148
a relevant policy provision or quietly rely on an altered application.

13
00:00:58.148 --> 00:01:03.368
Maryland also requires a prompt, reasonable explanation on request for

14
00:01:03.368 --> 00:01:08.508
a claim denial. Another section addresses specified unfair practices

15
00:01:08.508 --> 00:01:13.300
committed often enough to indicate a general business practice.

16
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.688
That includes repeated failures to investigate reasonably or

17
00:01:17.688 --> 00:01:22.788
respond promptly. Do not conclude that an isolated prohibited act

18
00:01:22.788 --> 00:01:25.968
becomes acceptable because there is no pattern.

19
00:01:27.008 --> 00:01:31.448
The two sections address overlapping conduct with different requirements.

20
00:01:32.568 --> 00:01:35.308
Identify the facts and the applicable rule.

21
00:01:36.242 --> 00:01:40.582
For life policies issued in Maryland, the basic interest rule runs

22
00:01:40.582 --> 00:01:42.662
from the insured's death until payment.

23
00:01:43.382 --> 00:01:47.162
The insurer need not pay interest if it pays the proceeds

24
00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:49.062
within thirty days after death.

25
00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:53.122
If proof of death arrives more than one hundred eighty days

26
00:01:53.122 --> 00:01:58.042
after death, interest instead runs from submission of that proof until

27
00:01:58.042 --> 00:02:01.682
payment. The rate is at least the rate payable on death

28
00:02:01.682 --> 00:02:04.022
proceeds left on deposit with the insurer.

29
00:02:04.702 --> 00:02:08.802
Maryland has corresponding individual and group life provisions.

30
00:02:09.502 --> 00:02:13.662
Keep this interest calculation separate from whether the underlying death

31
00:02:13.662 --> 00:02:18.208
benefit is payable. Now suppose the insurer fails financially.

32
00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:23.208
Maryland's Life and Health Insurance Guaranty Corporation exists to protect

33
00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:28.328
eligible people against specified failures of member insurers, within legal

34
00:02:28.328 --> 00:02:33.448
limits. It is a private, nonprofit, nonstock

35
00:02:33.448 --> 00:02:36.188
corporation, not a state department.

36
00:02:37.128 --> 00:02:40.700
Member insurers fund its work through assessments.

37
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.088
Depending on the circumstances, protection may involve continuing covered

38
00:02:45.088 --> 00:02:48.628
obligations or arranging a transfer to another insurer.

39
00:02:49.608 --> 00:02:54.088
Owners should follow the receiver's instructions and keep required premiums

40
00:02:54.088 --> 00:02:56.288
current to maintain coverage.

41
00:02:57.428 --> 00:03:01.888
Insolvency does not automatically make a policy free or turn every

42
00:03:01.888 --> 00:03:03.808
promise into a state debt.

43
00:03:04.646 --> 00:03:08.966
The Maryland life limits include up to three hundred thousand dollars

44
00:03:08.966 --> 00:03:12.266
in death benefits, with no more than one hundred thousand dollars

45
00:03:12.266 --> 00:03:15.466
in net cash surrender or withdrawal values.

46
00:03:15.926 --> 00:03:19.686
The annuity limit is two hundred fifty thousand dollars in present

47
00:03:19.686 --> 00:03:25.046
value benefits. These are statutory ceilings, not additional benefits

48
00:03:25.046 --> 00:03:26.266
added to the policy.

49
00:03:27.186 --> 00:03:32.966
Contractual obligations, eligibility, exclusions

50
00:03:33.186 --> 00:03:35.946
and the aggregate limit still matter.

51
00:03:36.846 --> 00:03:40.946
Multiple policies on one life do not multiply the protection.

52
00:03:41.946 --> 00:03:47.386
Investment risk borne by a policyholder and nonguaranteed portions are

53
00:03:47.386 --> 00:03:49.206
excluded under the stated rule.

54
00:03:50.106 --> 00:03:52.446
Check the complete contract and the law.

55
00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:59.460
A producer tells Elena to ignore an insurer's financial condition

56
00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:03.160
because guaranty protection makes the purchase risk free.

57
00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.800
That is wrong. Maryland prohibits using this protection in the sale

58
00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:12.860
of insurance. The law separately requires a written notice for a

59
00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.360
delivered contract that exceeds the stated limits or is outside the

60
00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:23.020
coverage, explaining those limits and the corporation's private status.

61
00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:27.540
A required disclosure is different from a sales inducement.

62
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:33.440
Explain the insurer, its actual promises and the product's risks

63
00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:38.640
accurately. Guaranty protection never replaces a careful,

64
00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.140
suitable coverage decision.
